      "stride": "Repudiation",
      "title": "No record of where a payment request came from, so disputes cannot be resolved",
      "scenario": "Because any website can trigger the link, a payment may be initiated by a page the user never consciously visited. With no record of the originating caller, referrer or link, the company cannot distinguish a genuine user-initiated transfer from a web-triggered one, and the user can plausibly deny authorising it. This makes chargeback and fraud investigation on this specific flow unresolvable.",
