        "when": "the user confirms it",
        "then": "the app sends the link source (calling package or referrer, where available), the raw link parameters and a flag that the flow was externally initiated, and the backend stores them with the signed user confirmation against the transaction"
      }
    },
    {
      "stride": "InformationDisclosure",
      "title": "Payee and amount leak through link handling on the device",
      "scenario": "Payment details are carried as query parameters in a URL. On the way to the app these values appear in browser history, referrer headers, OS link-handling logs, crash reports and analytics, and any other app that can observe or intercept the scheme sees who the user is paying and how much. An attacker with log access or a co-installed app builds a profile of the victim's payment relationships.",
